body:json {
  {
    "title": "The Importance of Consistency in Achieving Goals",
    "content": "Achieving goals requires more than just motivation—it demands consistenc. While motivation can be a powerful force that sparks our desire to take action, consistency is what sustains that action over time. The most successful individuals understand that showing up, even on days when you're not feeling motivated, is the real key to progress. Consistency builds discipline, fosters habits, and helps achieve measurable improvements. For example, a writer who commits to writing 500 words daily will accumulate thousands of words over weeks, while someone waiting for inspiration may lag behind. By breaking large goals into daily, manageable actions and committing to those actions consistently, we can steadily transform ambition into achievement. Although progress may seem slow at times, remember that every small step forward adds up to substantial growth over time. Remember, consistency is not about being perfect; it’s about not giving up.",
    "user_id": "18ed9e74-bd66-4581-96a8-529c216bdb0e"
  }
}
